  "term": "Librium",
  "definition": "Librium refers to chlordiazepoxide hydrochloride, a long-acting benzodiazepine with anxiety-reducing, sedating, and sleep-promoting effects. It acts in the central nervous system at benzodiazepine sites on GABA receptor complexes, increasing inhibitory activity.",
